<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">14 June in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">9 events that happened on 14 June, from 1158 to 1982.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1158">1158 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">868 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Henry the Lion wins the dispute over Munich at Augsburg</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">At <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/augsburg">Augsburg</a>, a dispute between Duke <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/henry-the-lion">Henry the Lion</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bishop">Bishop</a> Otto of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/freising">Freising</a> was settled in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/prince-henry-the-navigator">Henry</a>'s favour; the ruling named the place as forum apud Munichen. Henry had to pay the bishop a third of his income.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/munich">Munich</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/henry-the-lion">Henry the Lion</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1216">1216 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">810 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Prince Louis of France takes Winchester in the First Barons' War</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Prince Louis of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a>, who had invaded <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a> at the invitation of rebel barons, captured <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/winchester">Winchester</a>, abandoned by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/john-king-of-england">King John</a>. After John's death in October, many barons deserted Louis for John's young son Henry III.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/louis-viii-of-france">Louis VIII of France</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/winchester">Winchester</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/john-king-of-england">John, King of England</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/song-dynasty" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/song-dynasty.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1276">1276 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">750 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The exiled Song court crowns Emperor Duanzong in Fuzhou</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">In exile in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fuzhou">Fuzhou</a> from the advancing <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mongols">Mongols</a>, the remnants of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/song-dynasty">Song</a> court crowned Zhao Shi as Emperor Duanzong, the penultimate emperor of the Southern Song. Under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kublai-khan">Kublai Khan</a> the Mongols completed their conquest of the Song in 1279.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/song-dynasty">Song Dynasty</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mongol-conquest-of-the-song-dynasty">Mongol conquest of the Song dynasty</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fuzhou">Fuzhou</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1381">1381 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">645 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Rebels storm the Tower of London in the Peasants' Revolt</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Rebels of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peasants-revolt">Peasants' Revolt</a> stormed the Tower of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/london">London</a> and killed Simon Sudbury, Archbishop of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/canterbury">Canterbury</a> and Lord Chancellor, and Robert Hales, Lord High Treasurer. The same day the young Richard II met the rebels and promised reforms.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peasants-revolt">Peasants' Revolt</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1645">1645 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">381 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">New Model Army defeats Charles I at Naseby</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Fairfax and Cromwell's New Model Army destroyed the main royalist army in Northamptonshire. Captured royal letters damaged the king's cause, and the First Civil War was effectively decided.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1777">1777 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">249 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Congress adopts the Stars and Stripes</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The Flag Resolution called for thirteen stripes, red and white, and thirteen white stars on a blue field. The anniversary is celebrated in the US as Flag Day.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1800">1800 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">226 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Napoleon wins at Marengo</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Near defeat by the Austrians, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/napoleon">Napoleon</a> was saved by Desaix's arriving division, and the battle turned. The victory secured northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a> and his position as First <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/consul">Consul</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/napoleon">Napoleon</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/consul">Consul</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1940">1940 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">86 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">German troops enter Paris</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wehrmacht">Wehrmacht</a> marched into the French capital, which had been declared an open city. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> signed an <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/armistice-of-11-november-1918">armistice</a> eight days later.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paris">Paris</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1982">1982 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">44 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Argentine forces surrender at Port Stanley</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The surrender ended the 74-day Falklands War, in which 649 Argentine and 255 British service personnel died. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/argentina">Argentina</a>'s military junta fell soon after.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/argentina">Argentina</a></div></div></li></ol>
<section class="day-ppl" aria-labelledby="day-born"><h2 class="ref-sec-title" id="day-born">Born on 14 June <span class="n">5</span></h2><ul class="enc-seealso"><li><a href="/encyclopedia/ferdinand-ii-archduke-of-austria"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/ferdinand-ii-archduke-of-austria.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Ferdinand II, Archduke of Austria</span><span class="tp">1529–1595</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/frantisek-palacky"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/frantisek-palacky.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">František Palacký</span><span class="tp">1798–1876</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/marie-adelaide-grand-duchess-of-luxembourg"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/marie-adelaide-grand-duchess-of-luxembourg.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Marie-Adélaïde, Grand Duchess of Luxembourg</span><span class="tp">1894–1924</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/jose-carlos-mariategui"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/jose-carlos-mariategui.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">José Carlos Mariátegui</span><span class="tp">1894–1930</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/donald-trump"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/donald-trump.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Donald Trump</span><span class="tp">b. 1946</span></span></a></li></ul></section>
<section class="day-ppl" aria-labelledby="day-died"><h2 class="ref-sec-title" id="day-died">Died on 14 June <span class="n">8</span></h2><ul class="enc-seealso"><li><a href="/encyclopedia/emperor-qinzong"><span class="ph ph-person" aria-hidden="true"></span><span><span class="nm">Emperor Qinzong</span><span class="tp">1100–1161</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/gunther-von-schwarzburg"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/gunther-von-schwarzburg.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Günther von Schwarzburg</span><span class="tp">1304–1349</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/shibata-katsuie"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/shibata-katsuie.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Shibata Katsuie</span><span class="tp">1522–1583</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/orlande-de-lassus"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/orlande-de-lassus.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Orlande de Lassus</span><span class="tp">c. 1532–1594</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/jean-baptiste-kleber"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/jean-baptiste-kleber.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Jean-Baptiste Kléber</span><span class="tp">1753–1800</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/emmeline-pankhurst"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/emmeline-pankhurst.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Emmeline Pankhurst</span><span class="tp">1858–1928</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/jorge-ubico"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/jorge-ubico.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Jorge Ubico</span><span class="tp">1878–1946</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/jorge-luis-borges"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/jorge-luis-borges.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Jorge Luis Borges</span><span class="tp">1899–1986</span></span></a></li></ul></section>
<p class="day-ppl-note">Dates as the sources give them: in the Julian calendar before 1582, and in some countries for longer (Britain until 1752, Russia until 1918). Only people whose day of birth or death the records agree on are listed.</p>
